.TH TALONS 1
.SH NAME
talons \- first-person eagle fishing flight simulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/talons
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Talons
is a port of the TempleOS flight simulator of the same name.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
You fly first-person over a randomly generated island landscape of
water, grass, rock and snow, rendered in perspective with a sky and
ground horizon.
Dive down to the water: near the surface your speed steadies and your
claws reach down whenever a fish is ahead of you.
Fly over a fish to snatch it.
Catch ten fish as fast as you can; the best (lowest) time is saved
between runs.
.PP
Attitude controls the aircraft: diving builds speed and climbing bleeds
it, skimming the water pulls the nose up, and turning is done by
rolling and then pitching through the turn.
Flying into terrain \(em or off the edge of the map \(em ends the game.
Boats and trees decorate the landscape and flocking birds circle above
it; they are scenery.
.PP
The controls follow the original's airplane-style stick:
.TF space
.TP
.B Up / w
Nose down
.TP
.B Down / s
Nose up
.TP
.B Right / d
Roll right
.TP
.B Left / a
Roll left
.TP
.B Enter / r
Restart with a fresh map
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/talons.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR tone (2),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
The terrain is painted far-to-near rather than through a depth buffer,
so a tall tree or bird occasionally shows through a nearer hill.
The map is 512x512 cells to the original's 1024x1024; scenery densities
match the original per unit area.
